{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give SwiftUI views a tracker through the environment, and track what they do with view modifiers."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftuitracking"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"SwiftUITracking","title":"SwiftUITracking","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"SwiftUITracking"}],"role":"collection"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this module to track events from SwiftUI views on Apple platforms; elsewhere it builds empty."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Set a tracker once, at the root of the views, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and read it in any view below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Environment(\\.tracker)"},{"type":"text","text":". A button’s action can track through it, which a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binding can’t reach, since SwiftUI runs actions on tasks of its own. Until a tracker is set, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"environment’s tracker tracks through the one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.bootstrap"},{"type":"text","text":" made the process’s default, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with none it drops each event, warning once per call site. In a preview it is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.noOp"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a preview tracks nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The modifiers track through the environment’s tracker, once per trigger, and record the place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they are applied as the call site. "},{"code":"trackOnAppear(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks each time a view appears,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"trackOnTap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" each tap beside the view’s own action, and "},{"code":"trackChange(of:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" each new value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks "},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" each time the view appears, and puts a tracker enriched"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the screen’s "},{"code":"ScreenKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the environment inside it, so every event tracked from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"screen carries its name:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiftUI","import Traffluent","","@Event","struct CartOpened {}","","@Event","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","}","","struct CartView: View {","    @Environment(\\.tracker) private var tracker","","    var body: some View {","        List {","            Button(\"Check out\") {","                tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3))  \/\/ its record's context[ScreenKey.self] is \"Cart\"","            }","        }","        .trackOnAppear(CartOpened())","    }","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let root = CartView()","    .trackScreen(\"Cart\")  \/\/ tracks ScreenViewed(screen: \"Cart\") each time it appears","    .tracker(tracker)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apply "},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" where the screen’s view is placed, as above, not in the view’s own "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a view’s "},{"code":"@Environment","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads the environment around it, which its own body’s modifiers don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Where UIKit has traits, the environment’s tracker is the same value as UIKit’s trait"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), so SwiftUI views hosted in UIKit read the scene’s tracker. For UIKit and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"AppKit views, see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"To track screens without a modifier on each, see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The guide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers all three frameworks."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"API","anchor":"API","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s views aren’t there, so their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them for an Apple target. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" builds on every platform, as does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ScreenKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Events"},{"text":" module, so a tracking plan or a collector off Apple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platforms can name them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Setting the tracker","anchor":"Setting-the-tracker","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"EnvironmentValues.tracker","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"View.tracker(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Tracking from views","anchor":"Tracking-from-views","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"View.trackOnAppear(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.trackOnTap(_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"View.trackChange(of:_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Screens","anchor":"Screens","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.trackScreen(_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentati